ked into an AC: TM Wiki's shipped filterVisibleFacts (../TM Wiki/server/routes/characters.js:210-214) reads 'if (fact.st_hidden !== true) return true' - FAIL-OPEN - so any fact minted without st_hidden is silently visible to everyone; st_hidden is therefore required on every fact, costing nothing today since all 442 already carry it, and closing a real default-open hazard for every future writer. DELIBERATE NON-ENUMS with stated reasons: tag stays a plain string (DOSSIER_TAGS is a known-tag DRIFT-REPORTING set per _dossier-audit.js:13-14, not a rejection list - enum-ing it would contradict the script the export exists to serve), fact source stays a plain string (_rene-disambig.js:11 filters on source:'st', a value no live fact carries, so the vocabulary is demonstrably not closed), status stays a plain string (one live value 'outstanding', nothing reads it, a debt plausibly gains 'settled' later); severity IS enumed (minor/major/life_threatening, genuinely closed). Known transitional state, stated in the schema's own header rather than discovered later: required fact_key means all 442 live facts fail the schema until Angelus runs --apply, which is intended and visible - nothing validates this collection at runtime (no route, no DB validator), so required here is a documentation and test contract with no live blast radius. Residual hazard logged for deferred-work.md rather than scope creep: _havens-and-locations.js:46 $pushes new facts with no fact_key, the same class of finding dbo-1's own review made against seed-rules-necropolis.js. WHEN THIS LANDS AND ANGELUS RUNS --apply, TM Wiki must be told the mint is complete so they can backfill-verify and decide when to flip fact_level_enabled. DBO-7 (character_dossier/archive_documents handover) still depends on this landing first. Full story: dbo-2-character-dossier-schema-and-reveal.md. Prior entry follows. UNBLOCKED 2026-08-14 (Angelus's decision, via bmad-loop). Live-data check first: st_hidden:true is not concentrated on the 13 secret-tagged facts - all 26 tags, including plainly non-sensitive ones (aspiration, worldview, sire, haven, hunting_method), are 100% hidden across all 442 facts; zero carry any revealed_to entry; confirmed no server/routes/*.js writes character_dossier at all, only one-off server/scripts/_*.js tools. Presented as a genuine choice, not decided unilaterally - ANGELUS'S CALL: st_hidden:true as today's default is correct (he has not yet set what should be revealed, not that it must stay concealed forever), so a reveal writer does need building so he can set revealed_to per fact when ready. Scope now: (1) write the missing server/schemas/character_dossier.schema.js, closing the dead-citation bug cited by this repo's _dossier-audit.js:3 and TM Wiki's characters.js:219-220; (2) leave every existing fact's st_hidden value untouched, not a bug to fix; (3) build the missing reveal writer. Where that writer's UI should live (TM Suite admin vs. TM Cockpit, given the admin-to-Cockpit split direction) is still open - decide at create-story time. Ready for create-story. DBO-7 (character_dossier/archive_documents handover) still depends on this landing first. Old note follows: Two defects on one 30-doc/442-fact collection: server/schemas/character_dossier.schema.js does not exist despite two code sites (this repo's _dossier-audit.js:3, TM Wiki's characters.js:219-220) citing it as authority; and the reveal path was never wired - all 442 facts are st_hidden:true, revealed_to appears on ZERO of them, so the Wiki's summary tier shows nothing to any non-owner. NEEDS AN ANGELUS DECISION before any code: is full concealment intended, or is the mechanism simply unbuilt? Do not guess - a wrong guess leaks facts, and leaked facts are irreversible in players' heads. DBO-7 (character_dossier/archive_documents handover) depends on this resolving first.
