Pass 2 is complete. The safety guard around `tm_suite_test` is strong, and concurrent apply processes cannot both replace the same current slot because MongoDB evaluates `$exists:false` atomically. I found three repository-context issues: a legacy executable writer can recreate an unsafe/keyless haven fact, a mistyped database name can look like a clean database, and the DB test never proves preservation of an already-revealed fact. I’m freezing these now.

One disclosure already matters: a broad repository grep unexpectedly matched tracking files whose text embeds the author’s later account. I did not open the story itself, but that output contaminated the intended pre-record isolation. I’ll preserve the findings formed from code and report this exact protocol gap in the final attestation.
